//@ expect: accept
//@ reason: a field populated purely from a stored constructor parameter (no
//@ reason: other ownership signal -- no explicit @ptr hint, no back-reference,
//@ reason: no bidirectional assignment) must end up the SAME pointer kind as
//@ reason: whatever a fresh, unnamed `new T(...)` argument at a real call site
//@ reason: already defaults to. Found as a real, general, pre-existing bug
//@ reason: while developing closures (the same underlying gap as
//@ reason: inherit_inline_new_arg_constructs_declared_type_accepted.clg, but a
//@ reason: DIFFERENT symptom): SmartPointerAnalyzer::getPointerType's own
//@ reason: "not found" fallback is UNCONDITIONALLY SHARED (both its own
//@ reason: internal branches return PointerType::SHARED), so
//@ reason: `new Holder(new Dog())` always emits `std::make_shared<Dog>(...)`
//@ reason: for the argument -- but `secondPassDeterminePointerTypes`' own
//@ reason: base case for the FIELD that argument gets stored into is
//@ reason: `PointerType::UNIQUE` ("default unique ownership"), a completely
//@ reason: independent decision that was never reasoning about how instances
//@ reason: of this class get constructed at call sites at all. Left alone,
//@ reason: `Holder`'s constructor becomes `Holder(std::unique_ptr<Animal> c)`
//@ reason: while every real caller passes a `std::shared_ptr` -- a genuine
//@ reason: compile error (`no known conversion from shared_ptr<Dog> to
//@ reason: unique_ptr<Animal>`), not a safety hole, but exactly the "compiles
//@ reason: this pass, fails the next" gap the safety suite's own compile-gate
//@ reason: exists to catch. Fixed in
//@ reason: SmartPointerAnalyzer::promoteParamsInBody: when a field has NO
//@ reason: real signal of its own (checked via the reason string literally
//@ reason: being "default unique ownership", since pointerDecisions has an
//@ reason: entry for EVERY variable unconditionally and so cannot be used by
//@ reason: itself to detect "nothing decided this") and it's populated from a
//@ reason: stored parameter, the field is promoted SHARED to match. Must be
//@ reason: RUN, matching the same "compiles but does the wrong thing" concern
//@ reason: as the sibling fixture above (this one additionally confirms
//@ reason: correct virtual dispatch survives the promotion).
//@ run: woof

class Animal {
public:
    Animal() { }
    virtual void speak() {
        std::cout << "generic" << std::endl;
    }
};

class Dog : public Animal {
public:
    Dog() { }
    void speak() override {
        std::cout << "woof" << std::endl;
    }
};

class Holder {
public:
    Animal stored;
    Holder(Animal c) { stored = c; }
    void run() {
        stored.speak();
    }
};

int main() {
    Holder h = new Holder(new Dog());
    h.run();
    return 0;
}
